  "documentation": {
    "range": "This species is found in the interior of all eastern continental states of Australia, with ranges extending to the eastern half of South Australia and the southeast of the Northern Territory (Cogger 2014).",
    "population": "This species is locally common.",
    "habitats": "This species can be found in a range of habitats from dry sclerophyll forests, eucalypt and <em>Callitris</em>&#160;woodlands, mallee and acacia scrubs, to sandplain and sandridge deserts (Cogger 2014).",
    "threats": "This species is known to be preyed on by introduced foxes and feral cats (Read and Bowen 2001), but there are thought to be no major threats to the species.",
    "measures": "There are no species specific conservation action, however its range does coincide with multiple protected areas.",
    "use_trade": "This species and&#160;<em>Pogona henrylawsoni </em>are the most common agamid lizards&#160;the global pet trade (Ezaz <em>et al. </em>2005). It is widely captive-bred.",
    "rationale": "Listed as Least Concern on the basis that this species is very widespread and locally common. Although it is very common in the international pet trade it is very widely captive-bred and is not considered to be subject to major threats.",
    "trend_justification": null,
